cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DueCare in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "DueCare: A Gemma 4 safety ecosystem for migrant-worker protection"
abstract: >-
  DueCare is a local-first, open-source AI safety ecosystem built on
  Google's Gemma 4 that helps migrant workers, NGOs, regulators, and
  researchers identify recruitment fraud, contract substitution,
  passport retention, debt novation, and other trafficking-shaped
  patterns. The system serves six audience-facing lanes from one
  runtime: content moderation, case analysis, worker support,
  research, anonymized knowledge sharing, and custom API
  implementations. The harness composes deterministic GREP rules,
  audience-aware personas, vetted knowledge packs (ILO C029 / C181 /
  C189, Palermo, POEA, BP2MI, Nepal FEA, HK Cap. 57 / 163, SG EFMA,
  UAE MoHRE, RA 8042 / RA 10022), a BM25 RAG layer, a corridor-aware
  tool registry, optional online + official-source verification, and
  rubric grading on every response. Quantified result on the
  2026-05-18 e2b-full-train-eval smoke matrix (combined rule + LLM
  judge): Stock Gemma 4 2B 29.5%, Stock + chat-offline harness 35.6%
  (+6.1pp), Fine-tuned 26.4%, Fine-tuned + harness 41.2% (+14.8pp
  over fine-tuning alone, +11.7pp over stock). Bundled coverage:
  165+ deterministic rules, 55+ curated knowledge documents, 20
  migration corridors. Sensitive worker data stays on the worker
  device or trusted NGO hardware; the public hub only receives
  k-anonymous signals after explicit user action.
